# Telegram bot UI surfaces

Use these terms consistently in code, docs, and reviews. UI copy may differ by language.

## inline keyboard

Buttons attached to a **message** in the chat (not under the text field). Telegram: `InlineKeyboardMarkup`, `callback_query`.

## command menu

Primary bot flows entered via **slash commands** (e.g. `/start`, `/profile`). Not the reply-keyboard row under the input.

## reply keyboard

Buttons shown **under the message input** (composer). Telegram: `ReplyKeyboardMarkup`. Same idea as “footer menu” in informal naming.

## flow map

A visual map of how a process unfolds over time (actors, steps, branches). In this project, prefer **Mermaid** in chat (`sequenceDiagram`, `flowchart`, etc.) when the user asks for a flow map, mind map of a flow, or interaction diagram.

**User phrases:** “flow map”, “show the flow”, “mind map of the flow”, “sequence for …”.

**Not:** Telegram UI surfaces (inline keyboard, command menu, reply keyboard).
